    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-20T09:17:27+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-20T09:17:27+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-19T23:47:27Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-19T23:47:27Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A cold front will cross the west of the state this morning and will track across the east of the state during the day. Another high pressure system will move eastwards across waters to the south during Monday then over Victoria and the Tasman Sea on Tuesday. This high will extend a ridge westwards over SA ahead of a low pressure trough that is expected to move over the far west of SA during Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW008" description="Mid North" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-20T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-21T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-19T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-20T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the south at night. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds northwesterly 35 to 50 km/h turning southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the early afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures 25 to 31.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 3:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 7 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-21T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-22T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-20T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-21T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the early morning. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h turning southeasterly during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 15 and 19.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-22T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-23T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-21T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-22T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. The chance of morning frost in the east. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light during the day then becoming easterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 2 and 5 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 23.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-23T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-24T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-22T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-23T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming light during the afternoon then becoming northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
